    "body": "=== Regression ===\r\nWe found that the following commit causes a regression and it is fixed on the release v2025.14.2.\r\n063cbeaae Initial copy elision pass (#8042)\r\n\r\n=== Breaking changes ===\r\nNo breaking changes\r\n\r\n=== All changes for this release ===\r\n7cd8130e1 Support `expand` on concrete tuple values. (#8106)\r\n67a969206 Add new _getName to get extension decl names for core module docs (#7985)\r\n9ed7b5264 Add warning for comma operators used outside for-loops and expand expressions in legacy mode (#7984)\r\n063cbeaae Initial copy elision pass (#8042)\r\n9e2685853 export fewer things from module targets (#8089)\r\nd0848ab22 Run extras/verify-documented-compiler-version.sh only when built (#8097)\r\n1088e57b6 Add a new option to use hash for release-note script (#8096)\r\nf241b1438 Fix atomic fp16 vector SPIRV emit (#8104)\r\n631a4c37a Improve performance of AST deserialization (#7935)\r\nb9aad6649 Add Discord server link to Slang internal error messages (#8026)\r\nde7ccaf12 Fix unused space discovery for bindless heap. (#8075)\r\nb9f999b74 Enable on-demand deserialization of AST decls (#8095)\r\nb7039f0c9 Add `lock` file to `.gitignore` (#8029)\r\nb152f1bb1 Add back GFX smoke test (#8030)\r\nea600fa8f Document how to ignore tests (#8049)\r\ne0b912575 Fix GetDimensions to use mipLevel for SPIRV (#8065)",
